---
/** D13. /guides/best-romance-manhwa — see src/components/BestManhwa.astro. */
export const prerender = true
import BestManhwa from '../../components/BestManhwa.astro'
---

<BestManhwa
  slug="best-romance-manhwa"
  genre="Romance"
  keywords={['best romance manhwa', 'romance manhwa', 'best romance webtoons', 'romance manhwa to read', 'top romance manhwa']}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Romance is the genre manhwa does best. Korean webcomic apps built their audience on it, and it shows in the
      range: palace intrigue and villainess stories set in invented European empires, quiet campus and office
      romances, second chances, contract marriages and slow burns that take a hundred chapters to reach a first
      kiss. A lot of it is also hard to find legally, because only some series ever get an English licence.
    </p>
    <p>
      This list keeps to romance manhwa you can read on an official platform, ranked by what readers actually
      scored them. Every title links to its page, which names each platform and how much of the story is free.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Reading romance manhwa on the official apps</h2>
  <p>
    Romance is where the paid apps compete hardest. Tappytoon and Lezhin hold many of the licensed fantasy and
    historical romances, WEBTOON and Tapas carry a large free-to-start selection, and Manta charges one monthly
    price for its whole library. Many romance series on these lists are labelled "romance fantasy": the story
    happens in a fantasy kingdom, and the relationship is the plot. If you liked one, the title page shows similar
    picks, all with official links.
  </p>
</BestManhwa>
